---
title: Invite accept membership invariant
description: Domain rule — POST /auth/invite/{token}/accept must not overwrite an existing UserTenant row (owner protection + duplicate membership).
---

# Invite accept membership invariant

```yaml
id: INVITE-ACCEPT-MEMBERSHIP-INVARIANT
version: "2026-08-20"
status: LOCKED
authority: users-rbac.policy.ts · invites.service.ts
decisions: [DEC-P9-015, DEC-P9-018, DEC-P9-019]
related:
  - subphases/9.4-users-rbac.md
  - users-api-dispatch-addendum.md
```

## Problem

`acceptPendingInvite` historically **upserted** `UserTenant`:

- No row → create with invite role (correct).
- Existing row → **overwrite `role` + bump `sessionVersion` + force `ACTIVE`**.

That path bypassed `evaluateMembershipRoleChange` / `evaluateMembershipRemoval`. An owner could invite their own phone as `member` and accept — last owner destroyed without `transferWorkspaceOwnership`.

## Rule (domain)

Evaluated by `evaluateInviteAccept` in `users-rbac.policy.ts`. Enforced **before** persist in `acceptWorkspaceInvite` (`invites.service.ts`) and again inside both identity repositories (write-boundary race guard). Not a controller-only check. Not a second CASL matrix.

```text
existing UserTenant for (userId, invite.tenantId)?
  no  → create membership with invite role (admin|member|viewer)
  yes → reject; do not write role/status/sessionVersion; do not delete invite; do not append audit
```

### Case table

| Existing row | Decision | HTTP | Code |
| ------------ | -------- | ---- | ---- |
| None | **Allow** — insert membership, consume invite | 200 | — |
| `role = owner` (any status) | **Reject** — owner row unchanged | **403** | `INVITE_ACCEPT_OWNER_PROTECTED` |
| `admin` / `member` / `viewer` **ACTIVE** | **Reject** — duplicate membership; owner must PATCH role / DELETE / suspend explicitly | **409** | `INVITE_ACCEPT_MEMBERSHIP_EXISTS` |
| Same roles **SUSPENDED** | **Reject** — reactivate is `PATCH /users/{id}/reactivate` only, not invite accept | **409** | `INVITE_ACCEPT_MEMBERSHIP_EXISTS` |

Suspended is **not** an implicit reactivate. Invite accept is join-only.

### Cross-tenant

Lookup is `(auth.userId, invite.tenantId)`. Membership in workspace B does not block creating membership in workspace A. Workspace B row is not read or written.

```
User (global mobile)
 ├── UserTenant { tenantId: A, role: member }   ← accept invite to A creates this
 └── UserTenant { tenantId: B, role: owner }    ← untouched
```

## Non-goals (this change)

- No unique `(tenantId, phone)` on pending invites (P1).
- No invite TTL (P1).
- No Prisma migration / partial unique index on owner (P1).
- No UI copy or layout changes.

## Sequence

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant S as acceptWorkspaceInvite
  participant P as evaluateInviteAccept
  participant R as IdentityRepository
  S->>S: load invite + phone/tenant match
  S->>R: findMembership(userId, invite.tenantId)
  S->>P: existing role or null
  alt reject
    P-->>S: OWNER_PROTECTED or MEMBERSHIP_EXISTS
    S-->>S: throw InviteAcceptConflictError
  else allow
    S->>R: acceptPendingInvite (insert only)
  end
```
